  "notes": [
    "TIFF source decoder for the texture importer (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.10, stage A5f). Developer only: ImageCodec links it, runtime targets do not.",
    "LibTiff.Build.cs adds the Zlib include directory and consumer defines, because tif_zip.c includes zlib.h; consumers link LibTiff before Zlib. tif_zip.c passes its own zalloc and zfree (TIFF_zalloc through _TIFFmallocExt), as Z_SOLO requires.",
    "Allocation: tif_rocks.c defines _TIFFmalloc, _TIFFcalloc, _TIFFrealloc and _TIFFfree on a per-thread allocator binding (RocksTiffBindAllocator); without a binding every allocation fails. Rocks.patch moves the two CRT allocation sites (tif_hash_set.c, the IFD offset map in tif_dirread.c) to these functions, so no libtiff allocation reaches the CRT.",
    "Messages: the global handlers are null and ImageCodec sets per-handle handlers with TIFFOpenOptionsSetErrorHandlerExtR and TIFFOpenOptionsSetWarningHandlerExtR; nothing is printed. TIFFOpen and the other file open functions are not defined; ImageCodec reads from memory through TIFFClientOpenExt.",
    "In Debug builds (NDEBUG not defined) libtiff assert becomes the CRT assert. The asserts check internal invariants, not input data."
  ],
  "modifications": [
    {
      "file": "libtiff/tif_config.h",
      "upstreamSha256": null,
      "reason": "Hand-written configuration header in place of the file the libtiff CMake build generates from tif_config.h.cmake.in (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.10)"
    },
    {
      "file": "libtiff/tif_dirread.c",
      "upstreamSha256": "9a9220abd10e952c5147207461725630ccd9a0886e157ccabbe8c5a3006445fe",
      "reason": "Allocate the IFD offset map entries with _TIFFmalloc and free them with _TIFFfree instead of the CRT, so every libtiff allocation reaches the allocator bound in tif_rocks.c (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.10)"
    },
    {
      "file": "libtiff/tif_hash_set.c",
      "upstreamSha256": "f3d3aaf6ac8bfa79626e48fa4cc17c65abee3caa7577154370391c82a74120f4",
      "reason": "Allocate through _TIFFmalloc, _TIFFcalloc and _TIFFfree instead of the CRT (the IFD loop detection hash set), so every libtiff allocation reaches the allocator bound in tif_rocks.c (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.10)"
    },
    {
      "file": "libtiff/tif_rocks.c",
      "upstreamSha256": null,
      "reason": "Rocks platform layer in place of tif_unix.c and tif_win32.c: memory entry points through a per-thread allocator binding, null global message handlers, no file open functions (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.10)"
    },
    {
      "file": "libtiff/tif_rocks.h",
      "upstreamSha256": null,
      "reason": "Declaration of the tif_rocks.c allocator binding (RocksTiffBindAllocator) (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.10)"
    },
    {
      "file": "libtiff/tiffconf.h",
      "upstreamSha256": null,
      "reason": "Hand-written configuration header in place of the file the libtiff CMake build generates from tiffconf.h.cmake.in (lossless codecs, DEFAULT_EXTRASAMPLE_AS_ALPHA as in UE 5.8) (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.10)"
    }
  ],
